      "sc:author": {
        "@id": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0675-2847"
      },
      "sc:description": "Free browser-based DNA sequence editor and plasmid viewer. Opens, edits and saves GenBank, FASTA and SnapGene files and AB1/FASTQ sequencing reads; shows linear and circular maps; finds restriction sites, ORFs and CRISPR guides; designs and checks primers; aligns sequences and reads; and simulates cloning (restriction/ligation, Gibson, Golden Gate, Gateway). Everything runs in the browser: no account, no install, and files never leave the user's device.",
